# p01 nothing asserted (the open-world default)
#
# LinkML option: none. This is what a record looks like when option0 is not enforced, and what
# every other option degrades to if the reason is dropped.
#
# Present: examination 1 (from base.ttl) with Napoleon and the physician as participants.
# Absent: any height assay, datum, value, unit, or statement about why.
#
# A consumer can infer nothing about his height from this record: under the open-world
# assumption the missing triples may exist elsewhere. They cannot tell "not applicable",
# "not collected", "withheld", or "lost in transit" apart, and cannot tell this from p12
# (asked, answer unknown). The only triple this file adds is a human-readable comment.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/napoleon/> .

ex:examination1 rdfs:comment "Invented archive record. No height entry." .
    # no length measurement assay part, no measurement datum, no datum status
